Cron Job Format:

* * * * * command-to-execute
| | | | |
| | | | └── Day of the week (0 - 6) [Sunday = 0]
| | | └──── Month (1 - 12)
| | └────── Day of the month (1 - 31)
| └──────── Hour (0 - 23)
└────────── Minute (0 - 59)
------------------------------------------------------
Examples:
1️⃣ Run a script every day at 5 AM
0 5 * * * /path/to/script.sh

------------------------------------------------------
2️⃣ Run a script every Monday at 2:30 AM
30 2 * * 1 /path/to/script.sh

------------------------------------------------------
3️⃣ Run a script every 10 minutes
*/10 * * * * /path/to/script.sh

---------------------------------------------------------
4️⃣ Run a script on the 1st and 15th of each month at midnight
0 0 1,15 * * /path/to/script.sh

------------------------------------------------------------
5️⃣ Run a script every Sunday at 8 PM
0 20 * * 0 /path/to/script.sh
